<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saramaka</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saramaccan, Saramaka people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saramaka are a maroon people of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a>, descended from Africans who escaped from plantations in the late 17th and 18th centuries and settled along the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname-river">Suriname River</a>. After decades of war they won a peace treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colony in 1762. They keep their own political institutions and language, Saramaccan, and won a landmark land-rights ruling at the Inter-American Court in 2007.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saramaka.jpg" alt="Saramaka" width="320" height="570" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johnston, Harry Hamilton, Sir, 1858-1927 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saramaka-1910.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
